From 778e2f9854a168a9ee57bae501c02a8ea582bcaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Garfield <lucas@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:42:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add SPDX 2.3 counterparts of the ProdSec CycloneDX policies

Each CycloneDX policy in policies/cyclonedx gets an SPDX 2.3 policy in
policies/spdx with the same severities and one rule per CycloneDX rule:

- CDX_1_6_PLUS -> SPDX_2_3_PLUS (spdxVersion >= SPDX-2.3)
- CDX_ANCESTORS -> SPDX_ANCESTORS (ANCESTOR_OF / DESCENDANT_OF)
- CDX_VARIANTS -> SPDX_VARIANTS (VARIANT_OF)
- CDX_PROVIDES -> SPDX_PROVIDES (GENERATED_FROM / GENERATES)
- CDX_CPE -> SPDX_CPE (cpe22Type / cpe23Type externalRef on the described package)
- CDX_MULTICPE -> SPDX_MULTICPE (more than one CPE externalRef on it)
- CDX_MULTIPURL -> SPDX_MULTIPURL (a package with more than one purl externalRef)
- CDX_EXTERNALREFS -> SPDX_EXTERNALREFS (externalDocumentRefs: valid
  DocumentRef- ID and SHA1 checksum, non-empty spdxDocument, any present)
- CDX_MAINCOMPONENTDUP -> SPDX_MAINPACKAGE (every described SPDX ID is in
  packages[]; SPDX has no separate main component to duplicate)
- CDX_SBOMTYPE -> SPDX_SBOMTYPE: SPDX 2.3 has no SBOM type field, so this
  checks creationInfo.comment for "SBOM type: <CISA type>".

spdx_util.rego holds the shared helpers (described packages, refs by type,
relationships by type, spdxVersion as semver).
---
